    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18919" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Frūtis</span></b> , is (Etrusc. form
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fruti</span></b> ; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				v.
				in the foll.
			), f.
			an Etruscan modification of the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀφροδίτη</span>, <i>an Etruscan
				name of Venus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Veneri matri, quae Frutis dicitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 2, 14</span></i>
			.—Hence: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Frutinal</span></b> , ālis, n.:
			templum Veneris Fruti, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				90</span></i> Müll.</div>
